{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe heat here is stifling, but the spirit is invigorated. I spent the morning deep in the Esterhazy collection. The Prince, hearing of my presence, had his valet guide me through the private cabinet. It was a magnificent survey of the ethical life’s historical artifacts, though I found the arrangement somewhat arbitrary. I lunched with Sonnleitner and a Paduan professor; good wine, sharp conversation.\n\nEvening brought Rossini’s *Corradino*. The music is a torrent, overwhelming the intellect with pure sensation before reason can settle it. It is effective, certainly, but lacks the dialectical tension of true art. I am tired, yet the journey sharpens my thoughts. Think of me as I walk these imperial streets.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080350,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":173,"prompt_tokens":951,"total_tokens":1124,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-rDP2KEigQ1Uz1jOAGIsNT5FFkhUqtBtV","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":951,"prompt_ms":918.389,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9657087276550999,"prompt_per_second":1035.50891833417,"predicted_n":173,"predicted_ms":4173.051,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.261924418604654,"predicted_per_second":41.21684590003812}}